   rejected with an odd counterexample. Saying "holds for integers 0 ≤ k ≤ n, fails at n = -1" would help.
   (binom still prints as "binomnk": m10 is not fixed.)
G3 Minor. ∑ₖ binom(n,k) =? 2ⁿ gives "? (a side holds a calculus expression that is not evaluated yet)".

