NEW FINDINGS
------------
B1 (BLOCKER, pre-existing, same output on 8288a5e) Numerical integration prints answers whose own error estimate is
   about as big as the value. Answers are off by 10^4 to 10^16, shown with 10 digits.
   crates/mpp-core/src/calc/integrate/definite.rs:287 certified() returns 0 only when |v| <= err. Otherwise it returns v,
   however close err is to |v|. The steps show it, for example ∫_{10^7}^∞ atan(x)/x² dx: "≈ 1.095751607e-11 with
   estimated error ≤ 9.2e-12".
   Non-oscillating examples (the true value comes from mpmath):
     ∫_{10^7}^∞ atan(x)/x² dx          ≈ 1.095751607e-11    true 1.570796277e-7
     ∫_{10^9}^∞ atan(x)/x² dx          ≈ 1.095797858e-15    true 1.570796326e-9
     ∫_{10^12}^∞ atan(x)/x² dx         ≈ 1.095798325e-21    true 1.570796327e-12
     ∫_{10^7}^∞ 1/(x²+ln x) dx         ≈ 6.975771829e-12    true ≈ 1.0e-7
     ∫_0^∞ 1/((x+10^7)²+ln(x+1)) dx    ≈ 6.975771829e-12    true ≈ 1.0e-7   (so the start point is not the cause)
     ∫_{10^7}^∞ e^{-1/x}/(x²+ln x) dx  ≈ 6.975771131e-12    true 9.9999995e-8
   (10^0 to 10^6 are correct. The break is between 10^6 and 10^7. atan(x)/x² also has an elementary antiderivative,
   which the finite range uses, but the improper path never tries it.)
   Oscillating examples:
     ∫_{10^7}^∞ sin x/x² dx            ≈ -1.135429741e-12   true -9.072703021e-15
