     ∫_{-10^17}^∞ sin x/(x²+1) dx      ≈ -4.337847958e-32   true ≈ -8.86e-35
   Fix: apply far_tail to (-∞, -c] by reflecting x -> -x. For finite ranges with both ends far out, use the difference
   of two tails, or refuse. Refuse any oscillating integrand whose sampled range reaches |x| >= FAR, not just the last
   [c, ∞) piece. Bring the threshold below 1e8, or run the B1 accuracy gate, which would catch the 10^6 to 10^8 cases.

N6 (MINOR, new in 17aca0d) Non-oscillating trig integrands far out are now refused, with the wrong reason.
