NEW BLOCKER
-----------
R1. REGRESSION: trig of a huge number hangs with no time limit, in the CLI and in the IDE.
    Input:    $$ \cos(100000!) \approx ? $$   (also \cos(30000!), \cos(100000!) = ?, \sin(2^{1000000}) \approx ?)
    Observed: `mpp run` still running at 60 s (CPU spin, ~17 MB). In the IDE (file with that line plus
              "1 + 1 = ?"): open+settle times out at 30 s and no result appears, even for 1 + 1; each
              keystroke waits another 30 s. Typing does not cancel it. \tan(10^{100000}) takes 9.6 s.
              Pre-fix build (a6b9c78): the same inputs answer "≈ ? ✗ the value is undefined" in 0.09 s.
    Cause:    the new high-precision evaluator (8234824, crates/mpp-core/src/hp) does argument
              reduction at about log2(x) bits and keeps raising precision. hp/ has no deadline or cancel
              check, and sin_cos only refuses magnitudes above 2^20 bits.
    Found by: the 100k Session fuzz (first run hung on "\cos 100000!"), then confirmed by hand.
    Expected: a budget, deadline or cancel check in hp, or a lower magnitude cap, so it gives up within
              seconds with a clear message.

